course: dictionary
lesson: 2491
title: Deafness: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deafness is a noun, a thing a person can have. It means being unable to hear, or being able to hear only a little. The ending «-ness» turns the adjective deaf into a noun, so deafness is the state of being deaf.
explain: Read this sentence: «Most people who think they are "tone deaf" just have not practised.» The quote marks show that "tone deaf" is a special phrase, not a simple word. It describes someone who finds it hard to tell notes apart, so they may struggle to sing in tune. The writer adds that real tone deafness is rare.
explain: Deafness can also be figurative, which means it is a picture, not a literal ear problem. «Deafness to their pleas» means refusing to listen when people beg for help. Ask yourself: is the sentence about ears, or about someone choosing not to listen?
fact: Deafness means being unable to hear, or being able to hear only a little.
fact: Deafness can be present from birth, or it can come from illness, age or very loud noise.
fact: Many deaf people use sign language, such as British Sign Language or American Sign Language.
fact: «Partial deafness» means hearing only some sounds, and «total deafness» means hearing no sounds at all.
fact: Protect your ears from very loud noise, because loud noise can cause deafness.
exercise: What does deafness mean? | *Being unable to hear, or hearing only a little | Being very good at music | Speaking loudly to someone far away
exercise: What does «deafness to their pleas» mean? | *Refusing to listen to people who beg for help | Being unable to hear a loud bang | Singing very loudly in a choir
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means hearing no sounds at all. | partial deafness | noise-induced deafness | deafness in one ear | *total deafness
test: Which of these is a sign language? | *American Sign Language | Morse code | Pig Latin
test: Why are the quote marks in «most people who think they are "tone deaf"» important? | They mean the people are shouting | They are a spelling mistake | *They show that tone deaf is a special phrase, not the same as being unable to hear | They show the sentence is a question
exam: «Real tone deafness is rare.» If most people struggle to sing in tune, what should they do? | Shout louder when they sing | Stop listening to music | *Practise, because most people can learn to sing in tune with practice | Give up singing for ever
